<surname>Brown</surname><given-names>EN</given-names></name><name><surname>Ronda</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bright light induction of strong (type 0) resetting of the human circadian pacemaker</article-title><source>Science</source><year>1989</year><volume>244</volume><fpage>1328</fpage><lpage>1333</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2734611</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.2734611</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Minors</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Waterhouse</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Wirz-Justice</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A human phase-response curve to light</article-title><source>Neurosci Lett</source><year>1991</year><volume>133</volume><fpage>36</fpage><lpage>40</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1791996</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0304-3940(91)90051-T</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Eastman</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>High-intensity light for circadian adaptation to a 12-h shift of the sleep schedule</article-title><source>Am J Physiol</source><year>1992</year><volume>263(2 Pt 2)</volume><fpage>R428</fpage><lpage>R436</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1510182</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Shanahan</surname><given-names>TL</given-names></name><name><surname>Zeitzer</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Czeisler</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Resetting the melatonin rhythm with light in humans</article-title><source>J Biol Rhythms</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>